  "chapter": {
    "number": 4,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the End, a Song of David among the Psalms."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When I called upon him, the God of my righteousness heard me: you have made room for me in tribulation; pity me, and listen to my prayer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O you⌃ sons of men, how long will you⌃ be",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 6
          },
          {
            "text": "slow of heart? therefore do you⌃ love vanity, and seek falsehood? Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But know you⌃ that the Lord has done wondrous things for his holy one: the Lord will hear me when I cry to him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you⌃ angry, and sin not; feel compunction upon your beds for what you⌃ say in your hearts. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Offer the sacrifice of righteousness, and trust in the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Many say, Who will show us good things? the light of your countenance, O Lord, has been manifested towards us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have put gladness into my heart: they have been satisfied with the fruit of their corn and wine and oil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 7
          },
          {
            "text": "both lie down in peace and sleep: for you, Lord, only have caused me to dwell securely.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 6,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. heavy of heart.",
